exclusions:
  panel-datasource-rule:
    reason: >-
      Datasource UIDs are pinned on purpose. The dashboard mixes Azure Monitor
      (Log Analytics for KubeEvents and Resource Graph for the Flux extension
      state, both via azure-monitor-oob) with the four dis-core-<env>-products-amw
      Prometheus workspaces in one view, which a single template variable cannot
      express. A ${datasource} variable also saves the value "default"; the
      default datasource in dis-grafana-prod is Azure Monitor rather than
      Prometheus, so Grafana would silently bind the Flux timeline to the wrong
      Prometheus and render it empty with no error. See CLAUDE.md.
    entries:
      - dashboard: "Kubernetes Events"
  template-datasource-rule:
    reason: >-
      No datasource template variable by design; see panel-datasource-rule.
    entries:
      - dashboard: "Kubernetes Events"
